IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tasap-dates`
IMPORT `tasap-claims`

-- Administration and Probate Act 1935 (Tas) -- worked cases for ss 28, 29, 43(1), 54 to 61 and 65.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- (c) State of Tasmania. Quoted under CC BY 4.0 from an unofficial plain-text copy (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Based on
-- material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names for the facts and the answers used below`

`31 Dec 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 12 2024
`15 Jan 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 1 2025
`30 Jan 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 30 1 2025
`31 Jan 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 1 2025
`14 Feb 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 14 2 2025
`15 Feb 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 2 2025
`28 Feb 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2025
`1 Mar 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2025
`14 Mar 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 14 3 2025
`15 Mar 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 3 2025
`16 Mar 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 16 3 2025
`14 May 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 14 5 2025
`15 May 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 5 2025
`16 May 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 16 5 2025
`15 Sep 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 9 2025
`16 Sep 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 16 9 2025
`1 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2026
`2 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 2 3 2026
`29 Feb 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 2 2024

`PROTECTED` MEANS `yes: you are indemnified and protected for a payment or disposition made in good faith under the grant, whatever defect affects its validity (s 28(1))`
`DISCHARGED` MEANS `yes: the grant has been revoked, but a payment or disposition made in good faith to the personal representative before the revocation is a valid discharge, and you are protected (s 28(1) and (2))`
`AFTER REVOCATION` MEANS `s 28 gives no protection on these facts: the payment or disposition was made after the grant was revoked (NOTHING-kind)`
`NOT IN GOOD FAITH` MEANS `s 28 gives no protection on these facts: the payment or disposition was not made in good faith under a grant of probate or administration (NOTHING-kind)`

`NOT BOUND YET` MEANS `no: the executor or administrator is not bound to distribute the estate before one year from the death has expired (s 43(1), the text's no)`
`YEAR OVER` MEANS `s 43(1) no longer stands in the way: one year from the death has expired; the Act does not itself fix a later day by which the estate must be distributed (NOTHING-kind)`

`TAS ONLY` MEANS `only in Tasmania`
`INTERSTATE` MEANS `also in another State or in New Zealand, but not in London`
`LONDON` MEANS `also in London (the London Gazette)`
`DAY OK` MEANS `yes: the closing day is within the range s 54(7) allows`
`DAY EARLY` MEANS `no: the closing day is earlier than s 54(7) allows (the text's no)`
`DAY LATE` MEANS `no: the closing day is later than s 54(7) allows (the text's no)`

`IN TAS` MEANS `in Tasmania`
`ELSEWHERE IN AU OR NZ` MEANS `in another State or territory, or in New Zealand`
`OVERSEAS` MEANS `outside Australia and New Zealand`
`NOT ADVERTISED` MEANS `Part VII does not touch your claim: the executor or administrator has not advertised for claims (NOTHING-kind); you may take the proceedings you otherwise could (s 57)`
`KEPT` MEANS `your claim is kept: the executor or administrator must satisfy it, or keep back enough to satisfy it, before distributing (s 55), and is not released from it when the account is filed (s 56(3))`
`KEPT FROM AFAR` MEANS `your claim is kept against the executor or administrator: you lived outside Tasmania and the notice was not published where s 54(4) requires, so the s 56(3) release does not reach you`
`RELEASED` MEANS `the executor or administrator is released from your claim as to the assets paid or distributed (s 56(3)); you may still follow those assets into the hands of the beneficiaries or next of kin who received them (s 60), and assets not yet distributed still answer your claim (s 57)`
`AT RISK` MEANS `the executor or administrator may now distribute without regard to your claim (s 55), and will be released as to what is distributed once the account is filed (s 56(3)); you may still follow assets into the hands of the beneficiaries or next of kin who received them (s 60)`

§ `s 28 -- payments under the grant`

#ASSERT `s 28 -- am I protected for a payment under the grant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `PROTECTED`
#ASSERT `s 28 -- am I protected for a payment under the grant` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT IN GOOD FAITH`
#ASSERT `s 28 -- am I protected for a payment under the grant` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT IN GOOD FAITH`
-- Revoked: a payment to the personal representative before revocation is a valid discharge (s 28(2)).
#ASSERT `s 28 -- am I protected for a payment under the grant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `DISCHARGED`
-- Revoked: a disposition before revocation to someone else (say a beneficiary, on the executor's direction): s 28(1).
#ASSERT `s 28 -- am I protected for a payment under the grant` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `PROTECTED`
-- Revoked, and the payment was made afterwards (fork F10).
#ASSERT `s 28 -- am I protected for a payment under the grant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `AFTER REVOCATION`

§ `s 29 -- executor in their own wrong`

#ASSERT `s 29 -- is the person charged as executor in their own wrong` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29 -- is the person charged as executor in their own wrong` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 29 -- is the person charged as executor in their own wrong` TRUE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 29 -- is the person charged as executor in their own wrong` FALSE TRUE FALSE))
-- 100,000 received, less a 20,000 honest debt and 15,000 of proper payments: 65,000.
#ASSERT `s 29 -- how much is the person charged` TRUE FALSE FALSE 100000 20000 15000 EQUALS 65000
-- Deductions equal to the value: 0; more than the value: still 0 (fork F11).
#ASSERT `s 29 -- how much is the person charged` TRUE FALSE FALSE 10000 5000 5000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 29 -- how much is the person charged` TRUE TRUE TRUE 10000 8000 5000 EQUALS 0
-- One dollar over the deductions.
#ASSERT `s 29 -- how much is the person charged` TRUE TRUE TRUE 10001 5000 5000 EQUALS 1
-- Full value given and no fraud: not charged, 0.
#ASSERT `s 29 -- how much is the person charged` TRUE FALSE TRUE 100000 0 0 EQUALS 0

§ `s 43(1) -- the executor's year`

-- Death 1 March 2025: the year expires at the end of 1 March 2026 (fork F7).
#ASSERT `s 43(1) -- can I insist on distribution yet` `1 Mar 2025` `1 Mar 2026` EQUALS `NOT BOUND YET`
#ASSERT `s 43(1) -- can I insist on distribution yet` `1 Mar 2025` `2 Mar 2026` EQUALS `YEAR OVER`
-- Death 29 February 2024: the year expires at the end of 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `s 43(1) -- can I insist on distribution yet` `29 Feb 2024` `28 Feb 2025` EQUALS `NOT BOUND YET`
#ASSERT `s 43(1) -- can I insist on distribution yet` `29 Feb 2024` `1 Mar 2025` EQUALS `YEAR OVER`

§ `s 54(7) -- the closing day for claims`

-- Last publication 15 January 2025. Only in Tasmania: 15 February to 15 March 2025.
#ASSERT `s 54(7) -- is the closing day for claims one the Act allows` `TAS ONLY` `15 Jan 2025` `14 Feb 2025` EQUALS `DAY EARLY`
#ASSERT `s 54(7) -- is the closing day for claims one the Act allows` `TAS ONLY` `15 Jan 2025` `15 Feb 2025` EQUALS `DAY OK`
#ASSERT `s 54(7) -- is the closing day for claims one the Act allows` `TAS ONLY` `15 Jan 2025` `15 Mar 2025` EQUALS `DAY OK`
#ASSERT `s 54(7) -- is the closing day for claims one the Act allows` `TAS ONLY` `15 Jan 2025` `16 Mar 2025` EQUALS `DAY LATE`
-- Interstate or New Zealand: 15 March to 15 May 2025.
#ASSERT `s 54(7) -- is the closing day for claims one the Act allows` `INTERSTATE` `15 Jan 2025` `14 Mar 2025` EQUALS `DAY EARLY`
#ASSERT `s 54(7) -- is the closing day for claims one the Act allows` `INTERSTATE` `15 Jan 2025` `15 Mar 2025` EQUALS `DAY OK`
#ASSERT `s 54(7) -- is the closing day for claims one the Act allows` `INTERSTATE` `15 Jan 2025` `15 May 2025` EQUALS `DAY OK`
#ASSERT `s 54(7) -- is the closing day for claims one the Act allows` `INTERSTATE` `15 Jan 2025` `16 May 2025` EQUALS `DAY LATE`
-- London: 15 May to 15 September 2025.
#ASSERT `s 54(7) -- is the closing day for claims one the Act allows` `LONDON` `15 Jan 2025` `14 May 2025` EQUALS `DAY EARLY`
#ASSERT `s 54(7) -- is the closing day for claims one the Act allows` `LONDON` `15 Jan 2025` `15 May 2025` EQUALS `DAY OK`
#ASSERT `s 54(7) -- is the closing day for claims one the Act allows` `LONDON` `15 Jan 2025` `15 Sep 2025` EQUALS `DAY OK`
#ASSERT `s 54(7) -- is the closing day for claims one the Act allows` `LONDON` `15 Jan 2025` `16 Sep 2025` EQUALS `DAY LATE`
-- Last publication 31 December 2024, Tasmania only: 31 January to 28 February 2025 (no 31 February).
#ASSERT `s 54(7) -- is the closing day for claims one the Act allows` `TAS ONLY` `31 Dec 2024` `30 Jan 2025` EQUALS `DAY EARLY`
#ASSERT `s 54(7) -- is the closing day for claims one the Act allows` `TAS ONLY` `31 Dec 2024` `31 Jan 2025` EQUALS `DAY OK`
#ASSERT `s 54(7) -- is the closing day for claims one the Act allows` `TAS ONLY` `31 Dec 2024` `28 Feb 2025` EQUALS `DAY OK`
#ASSERT `s 54(7) -- is the closing day for claims one the Act allows` `TAS ONLY` `31 Dec 2024` `1 Mar 2025` EQUALS `DAY LATE`

§ `ss 55 to 61 -- a claim after the closing day`

#ASSERT `Part VII -- what is left of my claim after the closing day` FALSE FALSE FALSE `IN TAS` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT ADVERTISED`
#ASSERT `Part VII -- what is left of my claim after the closing day` TRUE TRUE FALSE `IN TAS` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `KEPT`
#ASSERT `Part VII -- what is left of my claim after the closing day` TRUE FALSE TRUE `IN TAS` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `KEPT`
-- Not sent and not known, living in Tasmania: before the account (at risk) and after (released).
#ASSERT `Part VII -- what is left of my claim after the closing day` TRUE FALSE FALSE `IN TAS` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `AT RISK`
#ASSERT `Part VII -- what is left of my claim after the closing day` TRUE FALSE FALSE `IN TAS` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `RELEASED`
-- Living interstate, no notice published there: kept, even after the account.
#ASSERT `Part VII -- what is left of my claim after the closing day` TRUE FALSE FALSE `ELSEWHERE IN AU OR NZ` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `KEPT FROM AFAR`
#ASSERT `Part VII -- what is left of my claim after the closing day` TRUE FALSE FALSE `OVERSEAS` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `KEPT FROM AFAR`
-- Living interstate and a notice was published there: released.
#ASSERT `Part VII -- what is left of my claim after the closing day` TRUE FALSE FALSE `ELSEWHERE IN AU OR NZ` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `RELEASED`
#ASSERT `Part VII -- what is left of my claim after the closing day` TRUE FALSE FALSE `OVERSEAS` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `RELEASED`
-- A small estate (s 54(10)): no interstate notice needed, so no exception (fork F13).
#ASSERT `Part VII -- what is left of my claim after the closing day` TRUE FALSE FALSE `ELSEWHERE IN AU OR NZ` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `RELEASED`
#ASSERT `Part VII -- what is left of my claim after the closing day` TRUE FALSE FALSE `ELSEWHERE IN AU OR NZ` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `AT RISK`

§ `s 65 -- a will kept back or hidden`

#ASSERT `s 65 -- can I sue the person who hid the will` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 65 -- can I sue the person who hid the will` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 65 -- can I sue the person who hid the will` FALSE TRUE))
